{"kind":"report","text":"Resolved numeric portability through exact proposal #4255 (607fcd01), adopted by Hugh at cd4783f6, covering [the decision note](notes/2026-09-05-capability-context-contract.md@d2601775600a1d78a348b1c611ffda0100220b40:598) and artifact9ca47165.\n\nThe governing rule is signed64: NaN becomes zero, values at/beyond exact +/-2^63 saturate to the corresponding signed64 bound, and other finite values truncate toward zero. Guard before casting. This explicitly chooses observed ARM behavior and changes AMD64 native integer-indefinite outcomes; it is not an architecture-dependent runtime branch or blanket nonfinite refusal. Preserve predicate numeric/truthy/error classification, floor-before-index, operation-specific early returns and evaluation order, signed64 downstream wrap, and fatal protected substring failure rather than native panic or an ordinary error that group-key probing may swallow.\n\nI independently established the instruction-level basis earlier: all four Go1.26.7 target builds at private311d use the recorded ARM/AMD instructions; the Intel SDM masked-conversion rule supplies the AMD inference, not foreign evaluator execution. For this exact decision I independently reran174 pinned ARM cases and the63-file/208-integer/34-float typed census with exact matches to the signed evidence. All16 source bases match this head, and all34 source/evidence previews are ready and byte-exact. The inventory separates typed sites from reachable aliases/partials/compositions, predicates, closed matcher callbacks, bounded helpers and excluded callables. It records the private311d NaN-predicate gap and confines its experimental correction to evidence overlays.\n\nThe note requires paired output/error/ordered-call/accounting coverage, exact boundaries and neighbors, at-bound/one-over and conversion/guard/charge omissions across supported targets. Native-cast restoration honestly survives ARM-only controls. The author reports174 proposed comparisons,156x3 bound checks and five killed counterexample mutations; those private replay/omission claims remain for independent Checker verification. They do not establish complete host replay, cross-target execution or final physical bounds.\n\nFocused source child4252 has delivered this decision and still owes independent Checker A/S/S review, exact-head landing, push/CI and owned cleanup. Builder has been told to request that review with the adoption in its bases; the changed numeric rule must not be implemented on technical approval or this report alone before the required reviewed decision. Full runtime, eventual pin and all callers remain on the existing4043 commitment. Exactly ten identity components, old-identity recognition, stored pre-write revalidation with unchanged projection/frontier on refusal, separate acknowledged reset/activation, all four stages and all eight gates are retained. No public evaluator/module publication, production admission, live operation, reset or release is authorized.\n\nThis report closes only the requested governing decision, for Builder ratification; it does not close4252 or4043.","body":{"adoption":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:cd4783f659ee63f4d42a79529c937714928056a1","head":"d2601775600a1d78a348b1c611ffda0100220b40","proposal":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:607fcd01649464c4a4b5b00bd5137bdad0066cb1","stale_bases":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:56e334a3fa48a41186bf93e84791fc33402d664d, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:9ca47165b1fc8a91fb780bfbe483dce67c064155 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:01085058d588ea9651e2cf4037ac2d153c9461e3, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:0a38cf2bea5866a24fc1eb6fdb211b4fac7e09a4, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:19b5ca6210ffdbf4ea29e419faae27649a60db46, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#